---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ContactBlock from '../components/ContactBlock.astro';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../data/schema';
import { contact } from '../data/contact';

const updated = new Date('2026-09-08');
---

<Base
  title="Privacy at Idea Collaborative"
  description="What this site collects, what happens to anything you send through a form, and who else sees it. Short version: very little, and nobody."
  path="/privacy"
  darkHero
  schemas={[breadcrumbs([{ name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' }])]}
>
  <header class="hero on-dark">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="chapter is-dark"><span>Privacy</span></p>
      <h1 class="display-lg">What this site <em>collects</em>.</h1>
      <p class="sub">
        Short version: very little, and nobody else sees it. The longer version is below, in plain
        words rather than the usual paragraphs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <Section surface="white" class="crumb-row">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' }]} />
  </Section>

  <Section surface="white">
    <div class="doc">
      <h2 class="display-md">Forms</h2>
      <p>
        When you send a form on this site, the fields you filled in are delivered by email to
        {contact.email} and stored by our form provider so the message is not lost in transit. That
        is the whole purpose. We use it to reply to you.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell it, rent it, or share it with anyone. There is no marketing list, no
        automated sequence, and no partner who receives your details. If you ask us to delete
        everything we hold about you, we will, and we will confirm when it is done.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md">Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        If analytics is running on this site it is a privacy-first, cookieless product that records
        aggregate page views and referrers. It does not set cookies, does not track you across other
        websites, and does not build a profile of you. That is why there is no cookie banner: there
        are no cookies to consent to.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md">Booking</h2>
      <p>
        The booking panel, once it is switched on, loads from a third-party scheduling provider and
        only when you scroll to it. If you book a time, the details you enter go to that provider
        and to us. Their privacy policy governs what they hold.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md">What we do not do</h2>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li>No advertising pixels, no retargeting, no social trackers</li>
        <li>No selling or sharing of anything you send us</li>
        <li>No email sequences you did not ask for</li>
        <li>No account required to read anything here</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="display-md">Children</h2>
      <p>
        This is a business-to-business site and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly
        collect information from anyone under 13.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md">Asking us anything about this</h2>
      <p>Email or call. A person answers.</p>
      <ContactBlock class="cb" />

      <p class="fine">
        Last updated {updated.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' })}.
        If this policy changes in a way that affects anything you already sent us, we will tell you
        directly rather than quietly editing this page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { background: var(--color-ink); padding-block: clamp(6.5rem, 5rem + 8vw, 9rem) clamp(2.5rem, 2rem + 3vw, 3.5rem); }
  h1 { margin: 0; color: #fff; }
  .sub { margin: 1.25rem 0 0; font-size: 1.0625rem; max-width: 38rem; }
  .chapter { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .crumb-row { padding-block: 1.25rem !important; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .doc { max-width: 42rem; }
  .doc h2 { margin: 2.25rem 0 0.6rem; color: var(--color-navy); }
  .doc h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .doc p { color: var(--color-slate); }
  .checks li { color: var(--color-navy); }
  .cb { margin: 1rem 0 2rem; }
  .fine { font-size: 0.8125rem; }
</style>
